use  you're going to carry that with you the  rest of your life you're going to think  back and wonder what else you could have  done to make that business ago you're  going to see other people capitalize on  the same idea and turn into successful  businesses and know that it could have  been you if you just tried harder and  you didn't give up you should not want  that life when Jeff Bezos started amazon  com he was 40 years old he was a VP at  an investment bank and he was the  youngest ever VP at the company and he  gave it up to start amazoncom the start  of calm company selling books people  thought it was crazy this was the early  early days of the internet said Jeff  what are you doing  you're on the fast track here  youngest-ever VP you're making tons of  money why do what he's getting rid of it  all to start a book company online  nobody's going to buy books online  you're crazy and even though may not  have made the most sense at the time one  of the main reasons that Bezos had to  keep going and he did it was because he  didn't want to live with the regret he  had to try he had to try because if he  didn't you would think for the rest of  his life I should have done that now  he's had a lot of success with amazon  com but in the early days nobody  believed in him and he kept going and he  gave up a successful life to do this you  never want to have an excuse any excuse  for seeing that you didn't give it your  best you didn't give it your all because  otherwise you're going to end up living  in regret for the rest of your life I  hope you guys have enjoyed today i hope  you'll apply the recipe for survival to  your business again we're looking to  follow our passion number one model  success number two don't quit number  three I always love hearing from you  guys I'd love to take some questions if  you want to leave it in the comments  below thank you so much i hope you apply  this to your business and I'll see you  guys soon  you
 

